Package: BayesClustNof1
Title: Bayesian Clustering and Hierarchical Models for Series of N-of-1 Trials
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("M. Abdullah", "Al-Mamun", email = "abdullah.al.mamun.stat@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Andrew G.", "Chapple", role = "aut"))
Description: Fits Bayesian models to series of N-of-1 trials with a common
    protocol. The home-host clustering model groups patients with similar
    treatment effects and borrows information mainly within groups; the
    hierarchical model with half-Cauchy priors on the between-patient standard
    deviations borrows from a common normal distribution. Both models include spike-and-slab
    priors for time, block and period effects and optional first-order
    autoregressive errors within treatment periods, and are fitted by Markov
    chain Monte Carlo samplers written in C++. The clustering model returns
    the posterior co-clustering matrix and the posterior distribution of the
    number of clusters, and a point estimate of the partition is available.
URL: https://github.com/abdullah-al-mamun-stat/BayesClustNof1
BugReports: https://github.com/abdullah-al-mamun-stat/BayesClustNof1/issues
